{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: none. The original program has no top-level data variable on the left side of a sampling statement; `N`, `t`, `x0`, `mu`, `gamma`, and `tau` are context inputs.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the loop of conditional normal sampling statements for the latent path with a single built-in `multi_normal` prior for the top-level parameter `x_free`. The multivariate normal mean and covariance are computed deterministically from the context data and are exactly the joint Gaussian distribution implied by the original linear Euler-Maruyama transitions. `x_free` is declared as a `vector[N]` so it can be the plain top-level left-hand side of `multi_normal`; the transformed parameter `x` is reconstructed deterministically. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N + 1] real t;

  real x0;

  real mu;
  real<lower=0> gamma;
  real<lower=0> tau;
}

transformed data {
  vector[N] x_mean;
  matrix[N, N] x_cov;
  array[N] real epsilon;
  array[N] real a;

  for (n in 1:N) {
    epsilon[n] = t[n + 1] - t[n];
    a[n] = 1 - gamma * epsilon[n];

    if (n == 1) {
      x_mean[n] = x0 + gamma * (mu - x0) * epsilon[n];
      x_cov[n, n] = square(tau) * epsilon[n];
    } else {
      x_mean[n] = x_mean[n - 1] + gamma * (mu - x_mean[n - 1]) * epsilon[n];
      for (k in 1:(n - 1)) {
        x_cov[n, k] = a[n] * x_cov[n - 1, k];
        x_cov[k, n] = x_cov[n, k];
      }
      x_cov[n, n] = square(a[n]) * x_cov[n - 1, n - 1] + square(tau) * epsilon[n];
    }
  }
}

parameters {
  vector[N] x_free;
}

transformed parameters {
  array[N + 1] real x;
  x[1] = x0;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    x[n + 1] = x_free[n];
  }
}

model {
  x_free ~ multi_normal(x_mean, x_cov);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":2,"gamma":4.430862487745358,"mu":2.6240231744734146,"t":[1.0,2.0,3.0],"tau":1.3778093594568723,"x0":3.5409584160258825}","protected_variables":[]}
